            "heading": "INT. HARPER HOUSE \u2013 KITCHEN \u2013 MORNING",
            "location": "HARPER HOUSE \u2013 KITCHEN \u2013 MORNING",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [
              "JAKE",
              "MAYA"
            ],
            "text": "JAKE HARPER, 34, stands at the coffee maker.\nNot unhappy.\nNot happy.\nA man who has gotten very good at occupying neutral\nterritory.\nHe pours two cups.\nOne black.\nOne with cream and two sugars.\nHe sets the second cup at the opposite side of the kitchen\nisland.\nA practiced gesture.\nAn old kindness.\nMAYA HARPER, 33, enters already dressed.\nProfessional even on weekends.\nPhone in hand.\nWork email open.\nShe is not cold.\nShe is tired.\n2.\nThere is a difference.\nJake slides the coffee toward her.\nJAKE\nCream. Two sugars.\nMaya looks up.\nAlmost surprised.\nMAYA\nYou remembered.\nJAKE\nEventually, yeah.\nA small smile.\nIt almost becomes something.\nThen it dies.\nThe kind of smile that used to happen automatically.\nNow requires effort.\nMaya takes the coffee.\nChecks her phone again.\nJake watches her for half a second too long.\nShe feels it.\nMAYA\nWhat?\nJAKE\nNothing.\nMAYA\nThat's never true.\nJake almost answers.\nDoesn't.\nInstead he looks out the kitchen window.\nAvoidance as muscle memory.\nSilence.\n3.\nNot hostile.\nWorse.\nPolite.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nYou grading today?\nJAKE\nSupposed to.\nMAYA\nMm.\nAnother silence.\nA marriage that has forgotten how to fight.\nJake stares at his coffee.\nThen, abruptly:\nJAKE\nLet's go somewhere.\nMaya doesn't look up.\nMAYA\nWhat?\nJAKE\nToday. Right now. Let's just get in\nthe car and drive.\nShe finally looks at him.\nTrying to read whether this is spontaneity, panic, or a\ndelayed homework assignment from couples therapy.\nMAYA\nDrive where?\nJAKE\nI don't know.\nMAYA\nThat is generally considered\nimportant information.\nJAKE\nAnywhere.\nMaya studies him.\n4.\nMAYA\nIs this because of therapy?\nJAKE\nMaybe.\nMAYA\nOur therapist said \"intentional\ntime.\n\" She did not say \"randomly\ndisappear into rural Tennessee.\n\"\nJAKE\nI heard nuance.\nMAYA\nYou heard the part where you didn't\nhave to plan.\nJAKE\nAlso that.\nFor the first time all morning, she laughs.\nA real laugh.\nTiny.\nBut real.\nJake notices.\nThe way a starving man notices food.\nMAYA\nYou actually planned this?\nJAKE\nFive minutes ago.\nMAYA\nWhich explains the confidence.\nJAKE\nConfidence is mostly just not\nthinking things through.\nMaya almost smiles again.\nThen her eyes drop to the phone.\nAn email notification appears.\nJake sees it.\n5.\nThe old version of him would have said something light.\nThe current version says nothing.\nMaya locks the screen.\nSets the phone face down.\nA decision.\nSmall, but not nothing.\nMAYA\nFine.\nJake blinks.\nJAKE\nSeriously?\nMAYA\nBefore I change my mind.\nJake smiles.\nA genuine one.\nThe first we've seen.\nCUT TO:",
