            "text": "Jake drives.\nMaya watches the scenery pass.\nFor a while, they simply exist together.\nComfortably.\nLike they used to.\n6.\nMusic plays low.\nNot their song.\nJust something old enough to feel shared.\nMAYA\nRemember Gatlinburg?\nJAKE\nWhich disaster?\nMAYA\nThe cabin.\nJAKE\nOh God.\nMAYA\nThe bear.\nJAKE\nThat bear broke into our honeymoon.\nMAYA\nTechnically, you left the cooler\noutside.\nJAKE\nThe bear was a criminal.\nMAYA\nThe bear was hungry.\nJAKE\nThe bear stole my hamburgers.\nMAYA\nThe bear stole your hamburgers\nbecause you challenged nature.\nJake laughs.\nMaya laughs.\nFor a moment they are themselves again.\nThen the laughter thins.\nSilence settles.\nNot painful at first.\nThen, slowly, painful.\n7.\nMaya looks out the window.\nJAKE\nWhat?\nMAYA\nNothing.\nJAKE\nAgain, statistically never true.\nMaya hesitates.\nMAYA\nI just forgot what this felt like.\nJake knows exactly what she means.\nThe silence after that says everything.\nHe looks ahead.\nKeeps driving.\nAvoiding the thing that would need to be said next.\nMaya lets him.\nFor now.\nA beat.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nYou ever notice how everybody wants\nto be understood?\nJake glances over.\nJAKE\nThat's a turn.\nMAYA\nI'm serious.\nJAKE\nI could tell by the sudden\nemotional danger.\nMaya smiles faintly.\nThen:\n8.\nMAYA\nEverybody says they want someone to\nreally see them. Really know them.\nJAKE\nOkay.\nMAYA\nBut the second somebody does...\nthey panic.\nJake keeps his eyes on the road.\nJAKE\nYou talking generally?\nMAYA\nMaybe.\nJAKE\nThat's ominous.\nMAYA\nIt's true.\nJake says nothing.\nMaya watches him.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nYou know, silence is also an\nanswer.\nJAKE\nI was hoping it was more of a\npause.\nMAYA\nYou use a lot of pauses.\nJAKE\nThey're affordable.\nShe gives him a look.\nNot cruel.\nAccurate.\nMAYA\nJake.\nHe tightens his grip on the wheel.\n9.\nJust slightly.\nJAKE\nI'm trying.\nMAYA\nI know.\nAnd that somehow hurts more than accusation.",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_005": {
            "scene_id": "scene_005",
            "heading": "EXT. BACK ROAD \u2013 AFTERNOON",
            "location": "BACK ROAD \u2013 AFTERNOON",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [],
            "text": "The highway gives way to smaller roads.\nThen smaller roads.\nThen roads that seem less maintained than remembered.\nThe sky slowly changes color.\nThe day getting away from them.",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_006": {
            "scene_id": "scene_006",
            "heading": "INT. SUV \u2013 MOVING \u2013 AFTERNOON",
            "location": "SUV \u2013 MOVING \u2013 AFTERNOON",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [
              "MAYA",
              "JAKE",
              "CUT TO BLACK."
            ],
            "text": "Maya glances at her phone.\nOne percent.\nMAYA\nYou know we're lost.\nJAKE\nWe're exploring.\nMAYA\nLost people always rename it.\nThe phone dies.\nBlack screen.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nFantastic.\nJAKE\nWe've got road signs.\nMAYA\nYou've ignored three.\nJAKE\nThey looked judgmental.\n10.\nShe shakes her head.\nBut she's smiling.\nThen she notices something ahead.\nOr rather behind.\nMAYA\nJake.\nJAKE\nYeah?\nMAYA\nYou missed the turn.\nJake looks.\nThe turn is already disappearing in the rearview mirror.\nJAKE\nDamn.\nMAYA\nYou always do that.\nJAKE\nDo what?\nMAYA\nDecide you're right before\nchecking.\nThe smile disappears.\nThe old argument arriving.\nJAKE\nWe're talking about a road.\nMAYA\nWe're never talking about the road.\nSilence.\nJake grips the wheel.\nThere it is.\nThe thing beneath the thing.\nHe could answer.\n11.\nHe could turn toward it.\nInstead, he looks ahead.\nOutside the windshield \u2014\nA narrow, unmarked road disappears into dense forest.\nJAKE\nI'll turn around.\nMAYA\nThere?\nJAKE\nLooks wide enough.\nMAYA\nJake\u2014\nBut he's already turning.\nThe SUV leaves the paved road.\nThe trees swallow them.\nAnd for the first time in the film \u2014\nsomething feels wrong.\nNot dramatic.\nNot supernatural.\nJust the faint sensation that the world has stopped being\ncasual.\nCUT TO BLACK.\nTITLE: THE SCENIC ROUTE\nFADE IN FROM BLACK:",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_007": {
            "scene_id": "scene_007",
            "heading": "EXT. FOREST ROAD \u2013 LATE AFTERNOON",
            "location": "FOREST ROAD \u2013 LATE AFTERNOON",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [],
            "text": "The SUV crawls down the narrow dirt road.\nTrees crowd both sides.\nThe canopy overhead thick enough to dim the sunlight.\nNo houses.\n12.\nNo fences.\nNo signs.\nNo power lines.\nNo tire ruts except their own.\nEven the birds have gone quiet.",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_008": {
            "scene_id": "scene_008",
            "heading": "INT. SUV \u2013 MOVING \u2013 CONTINUOUS",
            "location": "SUV \u2013 MOVING \u2013 CONTINUOUS",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [
              "MAYA",
              "JAKE",
              "CRACK.",
              "JAKE. GO."
            ],
            "text": "Maya watches the woods.\nMAYA\nThis doesn't feel like a\nturnaround.\nJAKE\nIt's a road. Roads go places.\nMAYA\nInspirational.\nJAKE\nThank you.\nMaya looks at the dash clock.\nThe numbers flicker.\nJust once.\nShe notices.\nJake doesn't.\nMAYA\nDid you see that?\nJAKE\nSee what?\nThe clock is normal again.\nMaya looks out at the trees.\nSomething about this place feels isolated in a way she can't\nexplain.\nWhich bothers her.\nShe is an engineer.\n13.\nExplanation is how she survives.\nAhead \u2014\nthe trees suddenly break.\nThe road opens into a wide clearing.\nJake slows instinctively.\nMAYA\nJake...\nThe clearing stretches perhaps two hundred yards across.\nSeveral vehicles.\nMen.\nEquipment.\nCrates.\nPortable floodlights mounted on towers.\nNot construction.\nNot logging.\nNot military.\nNot anything immediately recognizable.\nJake brings the SUV nearly to a stop.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nKeep driving.\nJAKE\nYeah.\nBut neither of them can stop looking.\nSomething is happening.\nA transaction.\nGroups moving methodically between vehicles.\nLarge black cases being transferred.\nNobody speaking loudly.\nNobody wasting movement.\n14.\nThe atmosphere feels formal.\nProfessional.\nOrganized.\nAnd wrong.\nMaya leans forward.\nMAYA\nWhat is that?\nJake squints.\nNear the center of the clearing sits a large matte-black\nvehicle.\nIts shape is difficult to process.\nAngular.\nGeometric.\nNot futuristic.\nNot sleek.\nSimply incorrect.\nLike the designer solved different problems than human\nmachines are built to solve.\nThe proportions bother Maya immediately.\nHer eyes move across it.\nRoofline.\nWheel placement.\nLoad bearing.\nAngles.\nEvery instinct she possesses starts quietly screaming.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nStop.\nJake stops.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nSomething's wrong.\n15.\nJAKE\nYou got all that from a parked car?\nMAYA\nLook at it.\nJAKE\nI'm looking.\nMAYA\nNo. Actually look.\nJake studies it.\nAt first he sees nothing.\nThen \u2014\nsomething.\nThe roofline.\nThe wheel placement.\nThe way the body seems balanced around a center of gravity\nthat should not exist.\nJAKE\nWhy does it feel weird?\nMAYA\nI don't know.\nThe answer bothers her.\nShe always knows.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nThe geometry doesn't work.\nJAKE\nGeometry?\nMAYA\nThe weight distribution should be\nimpossible.\nJake looks again.\nNow he sees it too.\nThe vehicle somehow appears balanced incorrectly.\nAs though gravity itself behaves differently inside it.\n16.\nNearby \u2014\na large crate opens.\nSeveral men remove objects from protective foam.\nWeapons.\nAt least they resemble weapons.\nLong.\nBlack.\nMechanical.\nExcept the grips are wrong.\nThe trigger spacing is wrong.\nThe proportions are wrong.\nDesigned for hands that aren't quite human.\nSilence.\nJake and Maya stare.\nNeither breathing.\nJAKE\nMaya.\nMAYA\nI know.\nJAKE\nTell me I'm imagining that.\nMAYA\nI can't.\nJake slowly shifts the SUV into reverse.\nCareful.\nQuiet.\nNobody has noticed them.\nNot yet.\nThe SUV begins backing away.\n17.\nTen feet.\nTwenty.\nThirty.\nMaya never takes her eyes off the clearing.\nThen something else catches her attention.\nThe people.\nNot all of them are people.\nAt least \u2014\nnot exactly.\nSeveral figures stand near the matte-black vehicles.\nTall.\nVery tall.\nWearing dark clothing.\nMotionless.\nToo symmetrical.\nToo patient.\nThe air around them seems oddly still.\nRain-dark clouds move overhead, but their clothing does not\nstir.\nMaya feels cold.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJake.\nJAKE\nDon't.\nMAYA\nThere are people standing by those\nvehicles.\nJAKE\nDon't say aliens.\nMAYA\nI wasn't going to.\n18.\nBeat.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nBut now I'm thinking it.\nThe SUV continues reversing.\nAlmost clear.\nAlmost gone.\nThen \u2014\nCRACK.\nA branch snaps beneath the rear tire.\nLoud.\nViolently loud.\nThe sound echoes through the clearing.\nEverything stops.\nEvery movement.\nEvery conversation.\nEvery transfer.\nTwenty heads turn.\nAll at once.\nToward the SUV.\nToward Jake and Maya.\nSilence.\nAbsolute silence.\nNobody shouts.\nNobody points.\nNobody runs.\nThat stillness is somehow worse.\nJake stares.\nThe people stare back.\n19.\nThen one of the tall figures slowly tilts its head.\nStudying them.\nNot surprised.\nInterested.\nInside the SUV, the radio crackles.\nStatic.\nNot from any station.\nA low, almost subsonic tone slips underneath it.\nMaya whispers:\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nGo.\nJake doesn't move.\nFrozen.\nThe figure continues watching.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJake.\nNothing.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJAKE. GO.\nThe spell breaks.\nJake slams the accelerator.\nThe SUV fishtails.\nDirt sprays.\nThe vehicle rockets backward down the road.\nInside \u2014\npure panic.\nJAKE\nWhat the hell was that?\nMAYA\nI don't know!\n20.\nJAKE\nWhat did we just see?\nMAYA\nI DON'T KNOW!\nBehind them \u2014\nnothing.\nNo pursuit.\nNo headlights.\nNo engines.\nJust forest.\nJake races through the trees.\nHeart pounding.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nMaybe it's military.\nJAKE\nMilitary doesn't build cars like\nthat.\nMAYA\nMaybe experimental.\nJAKE\nExperimental for who?\nMAYA\nI don't know!\nThe road twists.\nThe SUV nearly slides off the shoulder.\nJake corrects.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nSlow down!\nJAKE\nNo!\nThen \u2014\nthrough the rear window \u2014\n21.\nheadlights.\nFar behind.\nEmerging from the trees.\nOne pair.\nThen another.\nThen another.\nBlack SUVs.\nFast.\nProfessional.\nClosing.\nMaya sees them first.\nHer face drains of color.\nMAYA\nJake.\nJAKE\nWhat?\nMAYA\nThey're coming.\nJake looks.\nHis stomach drops.\nThree black SUVs.\nMoving with terrifying precision.\nNot reckless.\nNot desperate.\nCertain.\nAs though they already know exactly how this ends.\nJAKE\nOh God.\n22.\nThe chase begins.\nSMASH CUT TO:",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_009": {
            "scene_id": "scene_009",
            "heading": "EXT. TENNESSEE HIGHWAY \u2013 CONTINUOUS",
            "location": "TENNESSEE HIGHWAY \u2013 CONTINUOUS",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [
              "MAYA"
            ],
            "text": "The SUV bursts from the forest road onto open highway.\nJake jerks the wheel.\nTraffic swerves.\nHorns.\nThe vehicle straightens.\nThe black SUVs emerge seconds later.\nThen something unexpected happens.\nThey slow down.\nNo attempt to ram them.\nNo attempt to pass.\nNo attempt to stop them.\nThey simply fall back.\nWatching.\nFollowing.\nMaya notices immediately.\nAnd that scares her even more.\nMAYA\nWhy aren't they stopping us?\nJake doesn't answer.\nBecause he already knows.\nPeople who aren't worried about losing you are the most\ndangerous people in the world.\nCUT TO:\n23.",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          },
          "scene_010": {
            "scene_id": "scene_010",
            "heading": "EXT. HIGHWAY GAS STATION \u2013 EVENING",
            "location": "HIGHWAY GAS STATION \u2013 EVENING",
            "time_of_day": "",
            "characters": [],
            "text": "The station sits alone beside the road.\nFour pumps.\nOne service bay.\nA flickering OPEN sign fighting a losing battle against age.\nThe kind of place travelers forget five minutes after\nleaving.\nJake pulls in hard.\nThe SUV skids slightly.\nStops beside a pump.\nFor a second neither moves.\nBoth breathing hard.\nTrying to process what just happened.",
            "emotional_tone": ""
          }
