            "intent": "Maya watches the woods.\nMAYA\nThis doesn't feel like a\nturnaround.\nJAKE\nIt's a road. Roads go places.\nMAYA\nInspirational.\nJAKE\nThank you.\nMaya looks at the dash clock.\nThe numbers flicker.\nJust once.\nShe notices.\nJake doesn't.\nMAYA\nDid you see that?\nJAKE\nSee what?\nThe clock is normal again.\nMaya looks out at the trees.\nSomething about this place feels isolated in a way she can't\nexplain.\nWhich bothers her.\nShe is an engineer.\n13.\nExplanation is how she survives.\nAhead \u2014\nthe trees suddenly break.\nThe road opens into a wide clearing.\nJake slows instinctively.\nMAYA\nJake...\nThe clearing stretches perhaps two hundred yards across.\nSeveral vehicles.\nMen.\nEquipment.\nCrates.\nPortable floodlights mounted on towers.\nNot construction.\nNot logging.\nNot military.\nNot anything immediately recognizable.\nJake brings the SUV nearly to a stop.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nKeep driving.\nJAKE\nYeah.\nBut neither of them can stop looking.\nSomething is happening.\nA transaction.\nGroups moving methodically between vehicles.\nLarge black cases being transferred.\nNobody speaking loudly.\nNobody wasting movement.\n14.\nThe atmosphere feels formal.\nProfessional.\nOrganized.\nAnd wrong.\nMaya leans forward.\nMAYA\nWhat is that?\nJake squints.\nNear the center of the clearing sits a large matte-black\nvehicle.\nIts shape is difficult to process.\nAngular.\nGeometric.\nNot futuristic.\nNot sleek.\nSimply incorrect.\nLike the designer solved different problems than human\nmachines are built to solve.\nThe proportions bother Maya immediately.\nHer eyes move across it.\nRoofline.\nWheel placement.\nLoad bearing.\nAngles.\nEvery instinct she possesses starts quietly screaming.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nStop.\nJake stops.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nSomething's wrong.\n15.\nJAKE\nYou got all that from a parked car?\nMAYA\nLook at it.\nJAKE\nI'm looking.\nMAYA\nNo. Actually look.\nJake studies it.\nAt first he sees nothing.\nThen \u2014\nsomething.\nThe roofline.\nThe wheel placement.\nThe way the body seems balanced around a center of gravity\nthat should not exist.\nJAKE\nWhy does it feel weird?\nMAYA\nI don't know.\nThe answer bothers her.\nShe always knows.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nThe geometry doesn't work.\nJAKE\nGeometry?\nMAYA\nThe weight distribution should be\nimpossible.\nJake looks again.\nNow he sees it too.\nThe vehicle somehow appears balanced incorrectly.\nAs though gravity itself behaves differently inside it.\n16.\nNearby \u2014\na large crate opens.\nSeveral men remove objects from protective foam.\nWeapons.\nAt least they resemble weapons.\nLong.\nBlack.\nMechanical.\nExcept the grips are wrong.\nThe trigger spacing is wrong.\nThe proportions are wrong.\nDesigned for hands that aren't quite human.\nSilence.\nJake and Maya stare.\nNeither breathing.\nJAKE\nMaya.\nMAYA\nI know.\nJAKE\nTell me I'm imagining that.\nMAYA\nI can't.\nJake slowly shifts the SUV into reverse.\nCareful.\nQuiet.\nNobody has noticed them.\nNot yet.\nThe SUV begins backing away.\n17.\nTen feet.\nTwenty.\nThirty.\nMaya never takes her eyes off the clearing.\nThen something else catches her attention.\nThe people.\nNot all of them are people.\nAt least \u2014\nnot exactly.\nSeveral figures stand near the matte-black vehicles.\nTall.\nVery tall.\nWearing dark clothing.\nMotionless.\nToo symmetrical.\nToo patient.\nThe air around them seems oddly still.\nRain-dark clouds move overhead, but their clothing does not\nstir.\nMaya feels cold.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJake.\nJAKE\nDon't.\nMAYA\nThere are people standing by those\nvehicles.\nJAKE\nDon't say aliens.\nMAYA\nI wasn't going to.\n18.\nBeat.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nBut now I'm thinking it.\nThe SUV continues reversing.\nAlmost clear.\nAlmost gone.\nThen \u2014\nCRACK.\nA branch snaps beneath the rear tire.\nLoud.\nViolently loud.\nThe sound echoes through the clearing.\nEverything stops.\nEvery movement.\nEvery conversation.\nEvery transfer.\nTwenty heads turn.\nAll at once.\nToward the SUV.\nToward Jake and Maya.\nSilence.\nAbsolute silence.\nNobody shouts.\nNobody points.\nNobody runs.\nThat stillness is somehow worse.\nJake stares.\nThe people stare back.\n19.\nThen one of the tall figures slowly tilts its head.\nStudying them.\nNot surprised.\nInterested.\nInside the SUV, the radio crackles.\nStatic.\nNot from any station.\nA low, almost subsonic tone slips underneath it.\nMaya whispers:\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nGo.\nJake doesn't move.\nFrozen.\nThe figure continues watching.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJake.\nNothing.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nJAKE. GO.\nThe spell breaks.\nJake slams the accelerator.\nThe SUV fishtails.\nDirt sprays.\nThe vehicle rockets backward down the road.\nInside \u2014\npure panic.\nJAKE\nWhat the hell was that?\nMAYA\nI don't know!\n20.\nJAKE\nWhat did we just see?\nMAYA\nI DON'T KNOW!\nBehind them \u2014\nnothing.\nNo pursuit.\nNo headlights.\nNo engines.\nJust forest.\nJake races through the trees.\nHeart pounding.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nMaybe it's military.\nJAKE\nMilitary doesn't build cars like\nthat.\nMAYA\nMaybe experimental.\nJAKE\nExperimental for who?\nMAYA\nI don't know!\nThe road twists.\nThe SUV nearly slides off the shoulder.\nJake corrects.\nMAYA (CONT'D)\nSlow down!\nJAKE\nNo!\nThen \u2014\nthrough the rear window \u2014\n21.\nheadlights.\nFar behind.\nEmerging from the trees.\nOne pair.\nThen another.\nThen another.\nBlack SUVs.\nFast.\nProfessional.\nClosing.\nMaya sees them first.\nHer face drains of color.\nMAYA\nJake.\nJAKE\nWhat?\nMAYA\nThey're coming.\nJake looks.\nHis stomach drops.\nThree black SUVs.\nMoving with terrifying precision.\nNot reckless.\nNot desperate.\nCertain.\nAs though they already know exactly how this ends.\nJAKE\nOh God.\n22.\nThe chase begins.\nSMASH CUT TO:",
